  "info": {
    "contact": {
      "name": "zkvault",
      "url": "https://github.com/ahmedazizabbassi/pwd_manager"
    },
    "description": "\nBlind sync for [zkvault](https://github.com/ahmedazizabbassi/pwd_manager). The\nserver stores an opaque ciphertext blob per account and arbitrates versions\nbetween devices. It never receives the master passphrase, the vault key, or\nanything that can derive either.\n\n> **This page is a development-only affordance.** `/docs`, `/redoc` and\n> `/openapi.json` are all disabled when `ZKVAULT_ENVIRONMENT` is `production`,\n> `prod` or `staging`.\n\n## What the client computes before it talks to this API\n\n```\nmaster = Argon2id(passphrase, salt, ops_limit, mem_limit_bytes)\nauth   = BLAKE2b(master, \"zkvault/v1/server-auth\")   -> sent here, base64\nKEK    = BLAKE2b(master, ...) -- wraps the vault key, never sent\n```\n\n`auth_secret` is therefore a base64 string that decodes to **exactly 32 bytes**.\nThe server rejects anything else at validation time, which turns \"a client\naccidentally POSTed the real passphrase\" into a 422 rather than a breach. What\nis stored is `Argon2id(auth_secret)`, so a database dump yields neither the\npassphrase nor the key.\n\n## Trying it out from this page\n\n1. **POST `/api/v1/auth/register`** with an email, a base64 32-byte\n   `auth_secret`, and your KDF parameters. For scratch testing,\n   `python -c \"import base64,os;print(base64.b64encode(os.urandom(32)).decode())\"`\n   produces both the secret and (at 16 bytes) a usable salt.\n2. **POST `/api/v1/auth/login`** with the same email and secret. You get either\n   a token pair, or \u2014 if TOTP is enabled \u2014 `{\"mfa_required\": true, \"mfa_token\":\n   ...}`, which you exchange at `/api/v1/auth/mfa/verify`.\n3. Click **Authorize** and paste the `access_token`. Swagger UI is configured\n   with `persistAuthorization`, so it survives a page reload.\n4. **PUT `/api/v1/vault`** with a base64 blob and `base_version: 0`.\n\nAccess tokens last 15 minutes by design (there is no server-side revocation\nlist; `POST /auth/logout` revokes refresh tokens only). Refresh tokens rotate on\nevery use and reuse of a spent token revokes the entire family.\n\n## Conventions\n\n* **Errors** are `{\"detail\": \"...\"}`, except `409` on vault upload, where\n  `detail` is an object carrying `server_version` so the client can re-sync\n  without a second round trip.\n* **Concurrency** is optimistic. Send the version you edited as `base_version`\n  (and optionally the same number as an `If-Match` header); a mismatch is a\n  `409`, never a silent overwrite.\n* **Rate limits** are per IP and per route class, and return `429` with a\n  `Retry-After` header. The dev limiter is in-process, so it under-counts behind\n  multiple workers.\n* **`X-Request-ID`** is echoed on every response; send your own to correlate\n  with the server's access log.\n",
    "license": {
      "name": "MIT"
    },
    "summary": "Stores encrypted vault blobs. The server cannot decrypt them, cannot search them, and offers no password recovery.",
    "title": "zkvault blind sync",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/auth/kdf-params": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Public KDF parameters for an account, so a new device can derive its keys.\n\nUnknown accounts get deterministic decoy parameters instead of a 404: the\nendpoint must answer before authentication, so a truthful 404 would be a free\naccount-existence oracle.",
        "operationId": "kdf_params_api_v1_auth_kdf_params_get",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "description": "Account email. Unknown addresses get decoy parameters, not a 404.",
            "in": "query",
            "name": "email",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "description": "Account email. Unknown addresses get decoy parameters, not a 404.",
              "title": "Email",
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/KdfParamsOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          },
          "429": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Rate limit exceeded. Honour the Retry-After header."
          }
        },
        "summary": "Public KDF parameters for an account",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/auth/login": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Returns a token pair, or -- when TOTP is enabled and no `totp_code` was supplied -- an MFA challenge to redeem at `/auth/mfa/verify`. Unknown accounts and wrong secrets are deliberately indistinguishable, in body and in timing.",
        "operationId": "login_api_v1_auth_login_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LoginIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "anyOf": [
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TokenOut"
                    },
                    {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MfaRequiredOut"
                    }
                  ],
                  "title": "Response Login Api V1 Auth Login Post"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Unknown account, wrong secret, or wrong TOTP code."
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          },
          "429": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Rate limit exceeded. Honour the Retry-After header."
          }
        },
        "summary": "Exchange the derived secret for tokens",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/auth/logout": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Revokes every refresh token for the user.\n\nAccess tokens stay valid until they expire; keeping a revocation list for\nthem would mean a database read per request. The 15-minute TTL is the\ntrade-off, and it is the reason that TTL is short.",
        "operationId": "logout_api_v1_auth_logout_post",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/LogoutOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "401": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Missing, expired or rejected credentials."
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Revoke every refresh token for the account",
        "tags": [
          "auth"
        ]
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/auth/mfa/activate": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "mfa_activate_api_v1_auth_mfa_activate_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MfaActivateIn"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
